# docs/manual is NOT ignored: the `manual` build stage compiles it into the
# image so the app can serve the user manual at /manual/.

# The site time-clock agent. It runs on a PC in the customer's office, not in
# this image, and it depends on pyzk which has no business in the API. The
# Dockerfile already copies only backend/, frontend_src/, docs/manual/ and
# deploy/, so this is belt and braces against a future `COPY . .`.
